WEBVTT

00:27:57.583 --> 00:28:01.809
AG: Christiana Figueres
was a diplomat in Costa Rica for decades.

00:28:01.833 --> 00:28:05.851
In 2010, she landed a big role
with the United Nations.

00:28:05.875 --> 00:28:09.393
Her goal was to get governments on board
with the Paris Climate Agreement,

00:28:09.417 --> 00:28:14.101
a global deal to combat climate change
and invest in a low-carbon future.

00:28:14.125 --> 00:28:17.643
You know, the agreement
the US recently left.

00:28:17.667 --> 00:28:20.768
Now, negotiating with one
government is hard enough,

00:28:20.792 --> 00:28:23.726
but Christiana had
a few more parties at the table.

00:28:23.750 --> 00:28:25.309
CF: Yeah, 195.

00:28:25.333 --> 00:28:26.601
AG: Oh my gosh.

00:28:26.625 --> 00:28:27.893
CF: Sovereign governments.

00:28:27.917 --> 00:28:30.726
AG: So you're not just
negotiating with 195 people,